  "aiContextParagraph": "Pope Leo XIV’s official visit to Argentina has drawn significant public and media attention, highlighted by an open-air mass that attracted approximately 2.5 million attendees. Throughout his stay, the Pope has centered his discourse on economic policy, issuing rebukes against the austerity measures implemented by the administration of President Javier Milei. The pontiff argued that national economic progress must prioritize the welfare of all citizens, particularly the working class, while also defending the right to strike amid ongoing labor disputes. Beyond political engagement, the Pope’s schedule included private discussions with individuals who have survived clerical abuse, signaling a focus on institutional accountability. His arrival in Buenos Aires followed a recent diplomatic trip to neighboring Uruguay, marking a period of high-profile activity for the Vatican across the region.",
